WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.212
The easiest way to understand retrieval methods is to compare them on the same question.

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:14.682
We run dense search, BM25, and hybrid retrieval using the query about VPN, MFA, and a client update.

00:00:14.682 --> 00:00:18.427
Then we look at the top document titles from each method.

00:00:18.427 --> 00:00:23.492
Do not expect one method to win every time.

00:00:23.492 --> 00:00:26.607
That is exactly the point.

00:00:26.607 --> 00:00:28.682
[tts-break] A semantic question may favor dense search.

00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:33.567
A query with an exact identifier may favor BM25.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:39.142
Hybrid retrieval may provide a useful balance across a mixed workload.

00:00:39.142 --> 00:00:48.002
This comparison also introduces an important engineering habit: when you add a more complicated method,

00:00:48.002 --> 00:00:50.507
compare it against the simpler baseline.

00:00:50.507 --> 00:00:59.532
If hybrid retrieval does not improve your evaluation results, complexity is not automatically valuable.

00:00:59.532 --> 00:01:03.542
Use evidence from your own question set to justify the change.
